SfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"ADR 0106 pushed for review as Gerrit change 2400 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2400). Commit 2777ade999f4 on branch s0-adr-reclamation (off current origin/main, which already carries the merged W3 bridge d0bcd620 + the unrelated 0105 ssm ADR). Contents: new docs/adr/0106-remote-anchored-history-reclamation.md (Accepted); docs/concurrency.md §I1 .retired-lifecycle note promoted from follow-up to a specified model cross-referencing ADR 0106; regenerated docs/adr/README.md index + docs/adr/.numbers/0106 bijection marker. Plan-review PASSED + signed (verified_at_sha 64217d0) on the 5th round. make lint clean; all AC verification greps pass; check_adr_numbers.py + gen_adr_index.py --check pass. Awaiting LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 — NOT self-submitting per the epic's human-go/no-go discipline. Closing 866f (which unblocks e32d and the S1 collapse engine) is held until the change is Verified +1.","timestamp":1788051454186032039}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1787594744724752001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"c6c92aff-17a8-4f58-be32-06c155878d38","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"2da3-f375-03a4-4993"}],"description":"Author ADR 0106 defining **remote-anchored below-horizon HISTORY reclamation** whose PRIMARY lever\nis **commit/tree collapse** (retired-event GC is a secondary companion, not the pack lever), and\npromote docs/concurrency.md §I1 'permanent retention' (epic b306) from a follow-up note to an\nimplemented+cross-referenced model. This ADR is the causal-stability contract that unblocks S1-S3.\n(ADR number 0106 — 0105 was taken by an unrelated ADR that landed on origin/main.)\n\nScope (docs-only): the horizon config key (default 30d, portable, no CI-provider dependency); the\nremote-reachability computation (collapse checkpoint reachable from the sync remote's tickets ref\nfor >= N days); the stale-clone detection + FORCED remote-override protocol on reconnect (a clone\nwhose last convergence is older than N days overrides local with remote rather than reintroducing\npre-collapse history by rebase); the **C1-C5 causal-stability boundary at the commit/tree-rewrite\nlevel**; SNAPSHOT authorship_ledger carriage AND enforce_since re-anchor (both applied) for\nsignature/authorship verifiability; the portable rewrite primitive and per-backend publish-swap;\nand a proof that invariants I1-I9 still hold. State the accepted residual: a >N-day-drifted clone's\ndivergent local work is discarded. (Re-scoped 2026-08-29 from '.retired-only' to the\ncommit/tree-collapse lever - see epic comment 'Child-roster re-scope'.)\n\nNote: ADR numbering is a bijection — the ADR file is paired with a `docs/adr/.numbers/0106` marker\nand the generated `docs/adr/README.md` index, both DERIVED by `scripts/gen_adr_index.py` from\n`docs/adr/*.md` and checked by `scripts/check_adr_numbers.py` + `gen_adr_index.py --check` in the CI\ndocs-gates action (`.github/actions/docs-gates/action.yml`), NOT in `make lint`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] `docs/adr/0106-remote-anchored-history-reclamation.md` exists with the ADR shape (`# ADR 0106:`\n  title, `- **Status:**`, `## Context`, `## Decision`, `## Consequences`).\n- [x] The ADR defines the N-day horizon as a portable config key (default 30d, with a stated rationale)\n  and NO single-CI-provider trigger (the `project.portability` criterion applies).\n- [x] The ADR specifies remote-reachability (collapse checkpoint reachable from the sync remote tickets\n  ref for >= N days) and the stale-clone FORCED remote-override protocol on reconnect.\n- [x] The ADR states the C1-C5 causal-stability boundary at the commit/tree-rewrite level and how\n  signature/authorship verifiability is preserved (SNAPSHOT authorship_ledger carriage AND enforce_since\n  re-anchor, both applied).\n- [x] The ADR names the history-rewrite primitive as core-git (`git fast-import` / `mktree`+`commit-tree`,\n  NO third-party `git filter-repo`) and, per backend, the publish-swap: git-ref `--force-with-lease` CAS\n  for git remotes, and an exclusive push-locked bundle-set replacement bypassing the `git-remote-s3`\n  auto-doctor for the S3 backend — citing the auto-doctor never-discard-a-head resurrection hazard\n  (ADR 0093 / `src/rebar/_store/s3_doctor.py`) and proving its bypass safe under C1-C5.\n- [x] The ADR proves invariants I1-I9 hold under reclamation and names the accepted residual\n  (a >N-day-drifted clone's divergent local work is discarded).\n- [x] The ADR-number bijection artifacts are regenerated: `python scripts/gen_adr_index.py` creates the\n  `docs/adr/.numbers/0106` marker (content = the ADR filename) and adds a 0106 entry to the generated\n  `docs/adr/README.md` index; no ADR cross-reference dangles.\n- [x] `docs/concurrency.md` §I1 is promoted from 'follow-up' to implemented and cross-references ADR 0106.\n\n## Verification\n- `grep -n '^# ADR 0106:' docs/adr/0106-remote-anchored-history-reclamation.md` and\n  `grep -n '^## \\(Context\\|Decision\\|Consequences\\)' docs/adr/0106-remote-anchored-history-reclamation.md`\n  confirm the ADR shape and title.\n- `grep -nE 'I[1-9]' docs/adr/0106-remote-anchored-history-reclamation.md` (I1-I9 proof present),\n  `grep -nE 'C1|C5' docs/adr/0106-remote-anchored-history-reclamation.md` (C1-C5 boundary present),\n  `grep -n 'ADR 0093\\|s3_doctor' docs/adr/0106-remote-anchored-history-reclamation.md` (S3 hazard cited),\n  `grep -n 'force-with-lease' docs/adr/0106-remote-anchored-history-reclamation.md` (git-ref CAS named),\n  `grep -n 'discard' docs/adr/0106-remote-anchored-history-reclamation.md` (accepted residual stated).\n- `python scripts/gen_adr_index.py` then `python scripts/check_adr_numbers.py` and\n  `python scripts/gen_adr_index.py --check` pass (marker `docs/adr/.numbers/0106` present, README\n  regenerated, bijection intact).\n- `grep -n 'ADR 0106\\|implemented' docs/concurrency.md` confirms the §I1 promotion + cross-reference;\n  `grep -n '0106' docs/adr/README.md` confirms the index entry.\n- `make lint` passes (ruff/format only); `rebar review-plan unlikely-zealous-skua` re-run confirms the\n  plan is admissible.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"docs/adr/0106-remote-anchored-history-reclamation.md","reason":"New ADR defining the remote-anchored below-horizon history reclamation model: N-day horizon, remote-reachability, stale-clone forced override, the C1-C5 causal-stability boundary, SNAPSHOT authorship-ledger carriage, core-git rewrite primitive + per-backend publish-swap (git-ref CAS / S3 auto-doctor bypass), and the I1-I9 proof."},{"path":"docs/adr/.numbers/0106","reason":"ADR-number bijection marker (content = the ADR filename), generated by scripts/gen_adr_index.py and asserted by scripts/check_adr_numbers.py."},{"path":"docs/adr/README.md","reason":"Generated ADR index; regenerated by scripts/gen_adr_index.py to add the 0106 entry."},{"path":"docs/concurrency.md","reason":"Promote the I1 .retired/compaction 'permanent retention' note from a follow-up to implemented and cross-reference ADR 0106 as the reclamation model."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","536b-8930-b922-4063"],["relates_to","2da3-f375-03a4-4993"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"536b-8930-b922-4063","parent_status_uuid":"6113ba5e-2e7d-4fbd-ad09-537a4713df52","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"866f-440c-3686-42df","ticket_type":"task","title":"ADR: remote-anchored retired-event GC + stale-clone override (N-day horizon)","ve